page=f'''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Distant stock training collection</title><style>body{{font:17px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1000px;margin:35px auto;padding:20px;background:#101c29;color:#e5eef9}}td,th{{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #536276}}a{{color:#9cdaff}}</style><h1>Far-range training collection and verified offload</h1><p>29 October 2026 · collector-only update</p><p><b>Active:</b> capture starts at 180 nm, with dedicated stock training snippets independent of continuous RF quotas. Disk cap stays <b>5,000,000,000 bytes</b>; bulk saves remain every 12 hours. Readsb, DSP/neural decoder, relay, FR24 and ADS-B Exchange kept their processes/configurations/gain. Only far capture restarted, saving its previous RAM archive first.</p><h2>More useful distant examples</h2><table><tr><th>Policy</th><th>New behavior</th></tr><tr><td>Training packet source</td><td>CRC-valid DF17 from stock; original 2 ms UC8 waveform and exact Beast bytes/sample clock</td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>≥180 nm, causal stock position, NIC/NACp≥5, no MLAT/TIS-B, position age≤15 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Coverage</td><td>Separate 180–200, 200–250 and ≥250 nm quotas; up to 80 windows/hour each; time/aircraft diversity limits</td></tr><tr><td>RAM</td><td>48 MiB reserved for training, 128 MiB continuous RF allocation, existing 256 MiB batch bound plus existing bounded ring/history</td></tr><tr><td>Continuous RF</td><td>Hourly spread, about {s['capture_schedule']['hour_seconds']:.2f} RF seconds/hour; remains evaluation-only</td></tr><tr><td>Closing journals</td><td>Reserved closing-marker memory; never serialize open/unfinalized bursts</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Candidate labels remain ineligible until an independent no-correction readsb waveform replay agrees at the same timestamp on the Mac</td></tr></table><p>Training snippets do not consume the continuous RF quota, and snippets overlapping retained evaluation RF are skipped. External triggers and DSP/neural outputs never supply supervised labels. Archive schema is far-capture-v3, with training.uc8/training.jsonl checksums. The Mac qualifier emits the existing stock_crc_assisted format, subject to all later aircraft/payload/IQ/RF split exclusions.</p><h2>Data moved off SD</h2><p><b>{len(files)} saved archives, {total:,} bytes ({total/1e9:.2f} GB)</b>, copied or reused from an existing matching Mac backup, SHA-256 verified, made durable, then deleted individually on Pi only after rechecking its size, timestamp and hash. Mac path: <code>/Users/mit/Documents/!project/adsb-neural-rescue/data/raw/pi-offload-20261029</code>.</p><p>Saved RF/CRC archive directories are empty after the offload. This includes the archive created when the old collector saved its RAM at shutdown. Existing graphs, configuration and unrelated receiver files were not deleted. Live CRC RAM ({state['crc_ram_bytes']/1e6:.2f} MB at audit) and new capture RAM remain buffered for their normal save schedule; no decoder restart/forced CRC flush.</p><h2>Validation</h2><p>41 collection tests pass on Mac and Pi; 41 core tests pass on Mac. A destroyed temporary real-RF fixture with synthetic range metadata verifies end-to-end independent qualification; it is not counted as real distant training data. Protected services/configs, gain, sample counters and feeding pass the 90-second activation observation. No qualifying distant stock track was present during observation, so no future yield claim is made.</p><p>Rollback backup: <code>{html.escape(activation['backup'])}</code>. No neural model, DSP method or feed routing was changed.</p><p><a href="summary.json">Summary</a> · <a href="activation.json">Health/activation</a> · <a href="offload-final-state.json">Final SD/RAM state</a> · <a href="collection-tests-pi.txt">Pi tests</a> · <a href="qualification-fixture.txt">Qualification fixture</a></p>'''
